69
00:07:14,920 --> 00:07:19,900
Remember to scan for synonyms and choose the correct letter from the box.

70
00:07:25,980 --> 00:07:28,280
OK, let's check the answers.

71
00:07:29,220 --> 00:07:31,620
Question two, look at the grammar.

72
00:07:32,660 --> 00:07:39,440
Viewed as being more than, we need an adjective here to form a comparison.

73
00:07:40,560 --> 00:07:47,200
The text says street art feels more personal and conveys deeper meanings.

74
00:07:48,220 --> 00:07:54,600
In the word list, I, subjective, is the perfect adjective to describe something

75
00:07:54,600 --> 00:07:57,380
personal and open to interpretation.

76
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:06,360
Question three, the sentence is, improve the
blank of previously neglected neighbourhoods.

77
00:08:06,840 --> 00:08:08,760
Here, we need a noun.

78
00:08:09,700 --> 00:08:14,760
The text mentions turning overlooked areas into popular places.

79
00:08:15,940 --> 00:08:24,040
These changes improve the area's image, or
specifically its reputation, which is a noun.

80
00:08:26,260 --> 00:08:31,900
Question four, the summary says, financial benefits for blank.

81
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:40,580
After the preposition for, we need a noun or
noun phrase to tell us who gets the money.

82
00:08:41,900 --> 00:08:49,560
Paragraph five explicitly mentions an economic
impact that helps local shops and small businesses.

83
00:08:50,520 --> 00:08:55,940
This maps directly to the noun phrase, D, local businesses.

84
00:08:57,540 --> 00:09:01,260
Question five, many officials now give artists.

85
00:09:02,540 --> 00:09:06,860
We need a noun here to indicate what is being given.

86
00:09:07,960 --> 00:09:12,940
In the text, the officials are actively inviting artists.

87
00:09:13,900 --> 00:09:18,280
We need to change the action, inviting, into a noun.

88
00:09:19,420 --> 00:09:22,840
When you invite someone, you give them an invitation.

89
00:09:23,660 --> 00:09:28,020
So, G, invitation, is the correct noun.

90
00:09:28,860 --> 00:09:36,160
Question six, the verb have allowed is plural,
so we need a plural noun as the subject.

91
00:09:37,220 --> 00:09:41,380
Paragraph six says, technology has played a role.

92
00:09:42,340 --> 00:09:49,220
Looking at the list, A, technological advances, is the only plural noun phrase

93
00:09:49,220 --> 00:09:51,300
that matches technology.

94
00:09:52,320 --> 00:09:58,520
Question seven, this movement proves that, blank, should be available to all.

95
00:09:59,460 --> 00:10:02,500
We need a noun representing a concept.

96
00:10:03,460 --> 00:10:09,580
The conclusion says, it reminds people that creativity can belong to everyone.

97
00:10:10,460 --> 00:10:16,280
In this context, creativity refers to the ability to express art.

98
00:10:16,820 --> 00:10:20,160
This matches F, artistic expression.

99
00:10:20,680 --> 00:10:22,600
So, the answer is F.

100
00:10:29,870 --> 00:10:34,250
I hope that through these two videos, you have had a better understanding of

101
00:10:34,250 --> 00:10:35,570
